newline and in this order: the store's absolute root, A, the Goal's display id, `hyp-goal-run`, the stop clauses (the runner owes nothing; N non-retracted Results recorded under A in this Goal, N being 5 by default; it cannot take the next step honestly and says why), then the block's lines byte for byte. With no flag there is no branch or PR clause.\nEOF\ncat > l2.txt <<'EOF'\n[P] `--experiments N` sets N. `--branch B` and `--pr N` each add exactly one clause after the block, and each clause only narrows what the block allows. The output is the same for any order of the flags.\nEOF\ncat > l3.txt <<'EOF'\n[N] A body's block runs from its first line that starts with `May change:`, `Read only:` or `Never:` to the end, and is valid only if all three headings appear, each has text after it, and every non-empty line starts with one (headings are case-sensitive; a line of spaces, a tab or a lone carriage return is not empty). For a body with no valid block, `hyp prompt` exits 1, names the missing heading or the bad line, and prints no prompt on stdout.\nEOF\ncat > l4.txt <<'EOF'\n[P] `hyp add goal` with a body that has a heading but no valid block succeeds and warns on stderr, naming the rule; a body with no heading adds without a warning. Replay and `hyp check` report no error for either Goal.\nEOF\ncat > l5.txt <<'EOF'\n[N] `hyp prompt` writes nothing: the bytes of `.tree` are the same before and after. It carries no owner answer and no tree state beyond the Goal's id and body.\nEOF\ncat > l6.txt <<'EOF'\n[N] These exit 2: a missing or invalid actor, a branch that git refuses (such as one with a space), `--pr` or `--experiments` below 1, a repeated flag, an unknown node, and a node that is not a Goal. A run where no `.tree` is found exits 3.\nEOF\ncat > l7.txt <<'EOF'\n[N] In a store with two Goals, `hyp prompt` reads only the named Goal's body: the other Goal's block never appears in the output, and a Goal without a valid block is refused while the other Goal prints.\nEOF\ncat > l8.txt <<'EOF'\n[N] `hyp prompt` exits 1, naming the actor, when the actor already has a Result under that Goal.\nEOF\nwc -m l*.txt","description":"Draft Goal body and lines; check length and block rules"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3109,"cache_read_input_tokens":89661,"output_tokens":1672,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":61},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3109,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1672,"cache_read_input_tokens":89661,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3109},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":7967,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01E9hJ1qydiQw71Hgqg5PNgX":{"command":"mkdir -p $TMPDIR/g && cd $TMPDIR/g && cat > body.txt <<'EOF'\nBuilds `hyp prompt` for issue #113: hyp prints the /goal prompt for any Goal from the log, and a Goal body carries the run's constraints under May change:, Read only: and Never:. The candidate is a hyp commit. go test is the instrument, and skillcheck decides the skill text.\nDone means, by the owner on 2026-11-11: for a Goal with a valid block, the prompt carries every clause the hand-written run-5 prompt had, except the actor, the owner's answer, the branch, the PR, the commit and the run's own plan. A test pins this on a synthetic Goal under internal/cli/testdata. checkpoint-store:G-D1CH1R has no block, so hyp prompt refuses it and no test compares it.\nThe session settled that hyp prompt is a command that reads the log, and that no skill writes the prompt.\nMay change: the hyp repository, by commits on the l