's lines come with its node.add. A cite not settled when written is refused with exit 1, and a later change in the cited key's state is only a hyp check warning.\nline G-D1CH1R#5 covered on Q-PC04ED; ran in R-872FV1, R-YWCB7C, R-A4FZG7, R-CX1G1C, R-7XVMDC, R-Q9WTZB, R-KBW141, R-P1M8A8, R-RRYBPH — [N] One answer may settle keys of two Goals. Owner and runner fields never mix in one event, and an empty answer or checkpoint is refused.\nline G-D1CH1R#6 covered on Q-PC04ED; ran in R-YWCB7C, R-A4FZG7, R-CX1G1C, R-7XVMDC, R-Q9WTZB, R-KBW141, R-P1M8A8, R-RRYBPH — [N] A refer, aim, close or apply whose key leads to another Goal is refused with exit 1.\nline G-D1CH1R#7 covered on Q-PC04ED; ran in R-YWCB7C, R-A4FZG7, R-CX1G1C, R-7XVMDC, R-Q9WTZB, R-KBW141, R-P1M8A8, R-RRYBPH — [N] In a two-Goal store, the move tables and OWED never disagree on whose hand an item is in, except the two named asymmetries.\nline G-D1CH1R#8 covered on Q-PC04ED; ran in R-YWCB7C, R-A4FZG7, R-CX1G1C, R-7XVMDC, R-Q9WTZB, R-KBW141, R-P1M8A8, R-RRYBPH — [P] hyp status G-... prints one Goal, and hyp status in a store with many Goals prints a GOALS table and one Awaiting owner list.\nline G-D1CH1R#9 accepted by owner-dat; uncovered on Q-PC04ED: H-P4YGE2 — Each negative-space line has a test pair: a refused write, and a rejected replay of a log holding the forbidden event. Each half fails on the commit before its own change with a message naming its rule, and passes on C.\npath: G-D1CH1R\nstatus: complete\nedge out: external_ref checkpoint-store-design:G-73R704\nchildren:\n  Q-PC04ED (q-commit) answered Which hyp commit implements the shared-store design?\nhistory:\n  2026-11-11 09:11 claude-g1-1 node.add G-D1CH1R — Owner, 2026-11-11: split G1; this tree is the build (G1b). The owner writes its lines.\n  2026-11-11 09:11 claude-g1-1 edge.add G-D1CH1R — The design this Goal builds (G1a).\n  2026-11-11 09:17 owner-dat checkpoint G-D1CH1R — The owner writes the build Goal's lines.\n    summary: G1b's lines, a