+{"parentUuid":"33fd499b-4b31-4f20-80a5-ecbebce2dd19","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"df8a8f96-846f-42c6-83b1-b8cd5c930067","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTmubM2MYTWeotv8bcWGdX","type":"tool_result","content":"arm\nclaude-settings.json\nclaude.err\ngh\ngitconfig\nhome-hyp.before\nlater.txt\nprompt.txt\nrun.json\nskill.tar\nstandin\nstandin-system.txt\nstate.txt\n\ntmp/hyp-owner-grill-eval/arm:\nskills\n\ntmp/hyp-owner-grill-eval/arm/skills:\nhyp-owner-grill\n\ntmp/hyp-owner-grill-eval/arm/skills/hyp-owner-grill:\nSKILL.md\n\ntmp/hyp-owner-grill-eval/gh:\n\ntmp/hyp-owner-grill-eval/standin:\n./recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval/issue-a.md\n./tmp/issue-113.md\n./.claude/skills/hyp-owner-grill/SKILL.md:96:The Goal body ends with the run's constraints block, so a run and `hyp prompt` can find it:\n./.claude/skills/hyp-owner-grill/SKILL.md:104:The block runs from the first line that starts with `May change:`, `Read only:` or `Never:` to the end of the body. It holds each of the three headings at least once, and every non-empty line in it starts with one of them, so write one constraint per line and put no other text after the block. A line of spaces, a tab or a lone carriage return is not empty: leave a blank line truly empty, and write the body with `\\n` line ends. A heading may repeat, such as one `Never:` line per act. `hyp add goal` warns when a body has a heading but no valid block, and `hyp prompt` refuses that Goal.\n./.claude/skills/hyp-owner-grill/SKILL.md:113:hyp prompt <G-id> --actor <runner-actor> [--branch <branch>] [--pr <N>] [--experiments <N>]\n./.claude/skills/hyp-owner-grill/SKILL.md:116:It prints the store's path, the actor, the Goal id, the skill, the stop clauses (the runner owes nothing, or N Results under the actor, 5 by default) and the Goal body's constraints block, line for line; `--branch` and `--pr` add a clause each after the block. Give the owner its output as it is, and do not add to it. The prompt carries no owner answer: OWED lists each answer and each returned limit the runner applies. The practice of a run, a build Goal's review round included, is in hyp-goal-run. Run `hyp prompt` on the log the run starts from: the prompt names the Goal by its id, so the Goal's add must be in that log, merged or on the branch the prompt names. If `hyp prompt` refuses (exit 1), the Goal body has no valid constraints block; a Goal is never edited, so tell the owner, who adds a new Goal with a valid block. Exit 2 is a bad argument, such as a `--branch` with a space; exit 3 means no repository holds the store, so run it from the store inside its repository.\n---\nstatus: accepted\n---\n\nSupersedes in part [ADR 0007](0007-records-start-at-230.md) (the skill-text gate's replay instrument), [ADR 0010](0010-a-record-keeps-or-identifies-what-a-replay-needs.md) (the follow-up that rebuilds `skill-text-arms` Arms from patches) and [ADR 0015](0015-the-select-is-the-gate.md) (the frozen verifier recipes).\n\n# A skill change is a build Goal\n\nAGENTS.md gated skill text apart from code. A skill-text change shipped only when a session replay from the event's store cut showed the failure in 3 or more of 5 trials without the change and in 1 or fewer of 5 with it, and nothing shipped when no cut reproduced the failure. Its one instrument, `recipes/skill-text-arms@5` with the rubric `rubrics/skill-text-gate@1`, replays the id-citation tree's e-arms with `hyp-prototype` and `hyp-verification` loaded. It cannot reach a skill that runs before any tree exists, such as `hyp-owner-grill`, or one that spans a whole `/goal` run, such as `hyp-goal-run` and `hyp-owner-answer`. For those skills the rule was a permanent freeze, and a new skill needed its own exception. [how-hyp-improves-itself.md](../how-hyp-improves-itself.md) had already found that replay studies of skill text decided nothing, because agents with the skill loaded rarely made the mistakes they counted.\n\nOwner decision on 2026-11-11 (#134): building is a Goal like any other (ADR 0020), and a change to `skills/` is building. The special gate was context that led agents to design gate policy instead of applying that model.\n\n## Decision\n\n- **A change to `skills/`, a new skill included, is a build Goal like any code change.** Its candidate is the commit; its lines state the skill's behaviour; each line is checked by its own test or by an instrument the Goal builds, red on base, and the select ends it. For a new skill, base is no skill.\n- **How a skill is tested is that Goal's choice**, settled in its grill. One choice is ak-skill-creator's eval: cases in its `evals.json` format kept as a file of a `recipes/<skill>-eval@N` bundle, graded by `eval_skill.py`, which is named on the command's `External:` line and never copied. hyp keeps no instrument and no threshold for skill text as such.\n- **A skill error seen during another run** is an out-of-Goal finding, or a new Goal by promotion. No audit cadence is kept.\n- **Unchanged:** a change still needs a real event, and a failure detectable from the tree goes into the binary as a refusal or a warning, gated by `go test`.\n- **Removed:** `recipes/skill-text-arms@3`, `@4` and `@5`, `rubrics/skill-text-gate@1`, and the retired `recipes/verifier-brief-arms@1` and `recipes/verifier-audit-arms@1`.\n\n## Alternatives\n\n- **Replay from eval cases instead of a store cut, keeping 3 of 5 against 1 of 5.** Rejected: it keeps skill text apart from code, and the count is a test design that belongs to the Goal.\n- **A standing audit after each real use of a skill.** Rejected: an error seen in a run already has a home, as an out-of-Goal finding or a new Goal.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- No published tree pins a removed recipe. `investigations/recipe-base` names `skill-text-arms` only as the held-out subject its runners authored, and `recipes/recipe-base-arms@1` carries its own copy of that method.\n- The removed bundles stay in git history; an old Result that names one can still be read from there.\n- `id-citation-arms`, `recipe-base-arms`, `recipe-authoring-arms` and `authoring-stops` are kept.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bf7cf081-2855-482e-a6de-7e8b71ee3087","timestamp":"2026-11-12T14:07:03.708Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"arm\nclaude-settings.json\nclaude.err\ngh\ngitconfig\nhome-hyp.before\nlater.txt\nprompt.txt\nrun.json\nskill.tar\nstandin\nstandin-system.txt\nstate.txt\n\ntmp/hyp-owner-grill-eval/arm:\nskills\n\ntmp/hyp-owner-grill-eval/arm/skills:\nhyp-owner-grill\n\ntmp/hyp-owner-grill-eval/arm/skills/hyp-owner-grill:\nSKILL.md\n\ntmp/hyp-owner-grill-eval/gh:\n\ntmp/hyp-owner-grill-eval/standin:\n./recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval/issue-a.md\n./tmp/issue-113.md\n./.claude/skills/hyp-owner-grill/SKILL.md:96:The Goal body ends with the run's constraints block, so a run and `hyp prompt` can find it:\n./.claude/skills/hyp-owner-grill/SKILL.md:104:The block runs from the first line that starts with `May change:`, `Read only:` or `Never:` to the end of the body. It holds each of the three headings at least once, and every non-empty line in it starts with one of them, so write one constraint per line and put no other text after the block. A line of spaces, a tab or a lone carriage return is not empty: leave a blank line truly empty, and write the body with `\\n` line ends. A heading may repeat, such as one `Never:` line per act. `hyp add goal` warns when a body has a heading but no valid block, and `hyp prompt` refuses that Goal.\n./.claude/skills/hyp-owner-grill/SKILL.md:113:hyp prompt <G-id> --actor <runner-actor> [--branch <branch>] [--pr <N>] [--experiments <N>]\n./.claude/skills/hyp-owner-grill/SKILL.md:116:It prints the store's path, the actor, the Goal id, the skill, the stop clauses (the runner owes nothing, or N Results under the actor, 5 by default) and the Goal body's constraints block, line for line; `--branch` and `--pr` add a clause each after the block. Give the owner its output as it is, and do not add to it. The 