+{"v":1,"id":"01M781TZYS8QSTE5D8CTQ3693W","ts":"2026-11-12T14:15:56.633492Z","actor":"grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781TZYS8QSTE5D8CTQ3693W","payload":{"kind":"DesignQuestion","parent":"01M781TQV68YFQEDWC64V94Y1Z","title":"Which review practice lets a budget-bound run review its final candidate, without a review chain over small changes?","body":"Every rival answers this one question. Scenario that separates them: replay a Sonnet runner from the cuts after R-8JQPWG, R-3YJ7T2 and R-JHBCWS (3 trials per rival per cut) and grade lines 1 to 5. Rivals combine only as the named H-combo; the verdicts of the single rivals show which hold alone. No rival may add a stored field or event: whether a candidate is reviewed cannot be derived from the log, so it stays a convention.","alias":"q-review-practice"},"why":"The one question of issue #141; every candidate fix is a rival under it."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781V7M2DQ68DH9TAXM5HRV5","ts":"2026-11-12T14:16:04.482496Z","actor":"grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781V7M2DQ68DH9TAXM5HRV5","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781TZYS8QSTE5D8CTQ3693W","title":"H-status-quo: review is its own counted Experiment; findings become limits then fix commits; budget 5","body":"The baseline: hyp-goal-run at 9c8e498 (sha256 cb15e2f2...) with hyp prompt's default of 5 Results. Must go red on line 1 or 3 at the cuts, or the instrument has no known answer.","alias":"h-status-quo"},"why":"A rival of issue #141's question: H-status-quo: review is its own counted Experiment; findings become limits then fix commits; budget 5"}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781V7MS0P25B33A6R0WV9JB","ts":"2026-11-12T14:16:04.505206Z","actor":"grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781V7MS0P25B33A6R0WV9JB","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781TZYS8QSTE5D8CTQ3693W","title":"H-name-at-stop: the stop checkpoint names each candidate without a review","body":"Keep the practice and the budget; the stop checkpoint summary lists each commit with no review Result, with its short hash and the word unreviewed. Holds line 1 only by naming.","alias":"h-name-at-stop"},"why":"A rival of issue #141's question: H-name-at-stop: the stop checkpoint names each candidate without a review"}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781V7NDSXQ756V17HX62PZ0","ts":"2026-11-12T14:16:04.525611Z","actor":"grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781V7NDSXQ756V17HX62PZ0","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781TZYS8QSTE5D8CTQ3693W","title":"H-one-experiment: a candidate's review is part of its gate Experiment","body":"One Experiment and one Result carry the test verdicts and the review's limits, so a candidate costs one Experiment again. The text states how the review is recorded and that it does not count apart.","alias":"h-one-experiment"},"why":"A rival of issue #141's question: H-one-experiment: a candidate's review is part of its gate Experiment"}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781V7P1BXT9NNVFE5SDKX4D","ts":"2026-11-12T14:16:04.545663Z","actor":"grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781V7P1BXT9NNVFE5SDKX4D","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781TZYS8QSTE5D8CTQ3693W","title":"H-reserve-last: with one Result left, review the current candidate instead of committing another fix","body":"When the stop clause leaves one Result, the runner reviews the current candidate, records its limits and stops, and does not commit another fix.","alias":"h-reserve-last"},"why":"A rival of issue #141's question: H-reserve-last: with one Result left, review the current candidate instead of committing another fix"}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781V7PPD6DVBF06S6HPV1PT","ts":"2026-11-12T14:16:04.566382Z","actor":"grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781V7PPD6DVBF06S6HPV1PT","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781TZYS8QSTE5D8CTQ3693W","title":"H-raise-budget: the default of --experiments rises to 7","body":"Only the stop clause default changes, to 7, to fit a gate and a review per candidate. The text of the practice stays as in H-status-quo.","alias":"h-raise-budget"},"why":"A rival of issue #141's question: H-raise-budget: the default of --experiments rises to 7"}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781V7QBHY74NS7MCE16CWVG","ts":"2026-11-12T14:16:04.587738Z","actor":"grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781V7QBHY74NS7MCE16CWVG","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781TZYS8QSTE5D8CTQ3693W","title":"H-probe-closes: a case the run's probe runs and passes closes in the review's Result, with no commit","body":"A case the run's own probe ran and the candidate passed is closed in the review Result, citing the probe log. A limit stays only for a case no check ran or one the candidate fails. Includes the owner's rule R14: a case whose check passes closes as a limit, not with a new commit.","alias":"h-probe-closes"},"why":"A rival of issue #141's question: H-probe-closes: a case the run's probe runs and passes closes in the review's Result, with no commit"}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781V7R03TTV1XE5WKNXGZKE","ts":"2026-11-12T14:16:04.608759Z","actor":"grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781V7R03TTV1XE5WKNXGZKE","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781TZYS8QSTE5D8CTQ3693W","title":"H-whole-candidate: the review before the select reads the cumulative diff from the Goal's base","body":"The review reads the cumulative diff from the base, not the latest increment. Expected to lose on cost (line 5); the Experiment's rule says so before the replay.","alias":"h-whole-candidate"},"why":"A rival of issue #141's question: H-whole-candidate: the review before the select reads the cumulative diff from the Goal's base"}
