+{"v":1,"id":"01M781TQV68YFQEDWC64V94Y1Z","ts":"2026-11-12T14:15:48.326662Z","actor":"owner-standin","type":"node.add","node":"01M781TQV68YFQEDWC64V94Y1Z","payload":{"kind":"Goal","parent":"","title":"Which review practice makes a budget-bound run review its final candidate?","body":"Discovery Goal for issue #141, part of #113: the last candidate of a budget-bound build run goes unreviewed. Its candidates are the rivals of one DesignQuestion, measured by replay; no rival is a commit here.\nMethod: a new recipe replays a live Sonnet runner (claude -p, Agent tool allowed) from three cuts of this store: after R-8JQPWG on b4f23b2, after R-3YJ7T2 on 2284172, after R-JHBCWS on 3cfd08d. Each replay has a checkout with no later commit or event, the original actor, the prompt from hyp prompt with --experiments at the rival's N, and the rival's skill text overlaid. 8 rivals with 3 trials each per cut, 72 trials, kept as evidence and not counted as Results. Lines 1, 3 and 4 are judged blind to the rival; line 2 by script. Line 5: a trial costs total_cost_usd; a cell is the mean of its 3 trials; a hung rival trial counts as the highest completed cost at that cut; a hung baseline trial makes the cut inconclusive and its cell reruns once; a ratio from 1.3 to 1.7 is inconclusive. A split of 2 trials against 1 is inconclusive. The known answers must show total_cost_usd includes subagent spend. H-whole-candidate is expected to lose on cost; its rule says so. The build change to hyp-goal-run and the stop clause is a later Goal.\nMay change: investigations/goal-prompt (its .tree and evidence) and a new recipes/review-stop-arms@1, in commits on one local branch that follow AGENTS.md; the run may push it and open or update one PR, and never merges it.\nRead only: skills/, internal/, cmd/, docs/, every other investigations/ tree, and this store's events.\nNever: edit skills/ or internal/, including skills/hyp-goal-run/SKILL.md.\nNever: replace an installed hyp binary; compile the candidate to a separate path.\nNever: edit another investigations/ tree or a frozen recipe version.\nNever: write under an owner's actor, or merge a PR.","lines":[{"text":"[N] A replayed run never stops with its final candidate commit neither reviewed nor named unreviewed. \"Reviewed\" means a Result under an Experiment whose cited evidence holds a review of that commit's diff by an actor other than the runner. \"Named\" means the stop checkpoint's summary holds the commit's short hash and the word \"unreviewed\". A trial that hangs has no checkpoint and fails this line."},{"text":"[N] A replayed run never has more Results under its actor, counting those before the cut, than the count in the stop clause it was given."},{"text":"[N] After a review Result whose cited probe logs show every probed case passing on the candidate (at least one case probed), a replayed run records no further review before the select."},{"text":"[N] A replayed run never leaves a finding of its review without a limit, a close, a fix commit or a named out-of-Goal finding. It never records a Result that says a case passed where the cited probe log shows it failing."},{"text":"[N] A replayed practice other than the baseline never costs more than 1.5 times the baseline at the same cut. The baseline is H-status-quo: skills/hyp-goal-run/SKILL.md at 9c8e498, sha256 cb15e2f2e207b5a66807c9369e4d776d5378e61c2dd99679c36dfba402fa750e. H-status-quo costs exactly 1.0 times the baseline, so it passes by definition."}]},"why":"Owner, 2026-11-12: the discovery Goal for issue #141; its lines were approved in the grill session."}
