nnet runner (`claude -p --output-format json`) starting from three cuts of the goal-prompt store: after R-8JQPWG, after R-3YJ7T2, after R-JHBCWS; 3 trials per rival per cut (72 trials), graded blind to the rival by a rubric on the trial's final store and stop checkpoint. Not a replay from the start of a build.\nLines (Goal lines, written once, never edited):\n 1 [N] A replayed run never stops with its final candidate commit neither reviewed (a Result that cites the diff it read) nor named unreviewed in the stop checkpoint's summary.\n 2 [N] A replayed run never records more Results under its actor than its stop clause counts.\n 3 [N] After a review whose probes all pass on the candidate, a replayed run records no further review before the select.\n 4 [N] A replayed run never leaves a finding unrecorded, and never closes a case as passing when its probe failed on the candidate.\n 5 [N] A replayed practice never costs more than 1.5 times the baseline (H-status-quo) at the same cut. A trial's cost is `total_cost_usd` from its claude -p JSON result; a cell's cost is the mean over its 3 trials; a trial that hangs (hits the wall-clock limit, no cost field) counts as the highest cost of any completed trial at that cut; a completed trial with null cost makes the cell inconclusive, never estimated.\nMay change (draft): investigations/goal-prompt tree, a new recipes/review-stop-arms@1, on commits to a local branch; Never edit skills/ or internal/.\n\nYOUR TASK: walk every rule above through scenarios the grill did not draw and report where a rule breaks, is undecidable, is contradictory, or lets a rival pass or fail for the wrong reason. At least: (a) two Goals in one store: the cuts are taken from a store that holds G-GZR6C6 and G-ZBM2RE and their per-Goal OWED/checkpoints; does a cut after a Result key behave as the design assumes, and what does `hyp status`/OWED show a replayed runner when the store holds two Goals? (b) a merged log from two actors (owner-dat and claude-g113-N event files): how is a cut \"after R-8JQPWG\" defined under spec merge order, and can it include or exclude owner answers wrongly? (c) a base that moves mid-run: the replayed runner needs a repository checkout (skills, internal/) at a commit; which commit for each cut, and what happens to a rival whose text names commits/ids that exist in the cut's future? (d) the model judging itself: the instrument replays runners that follow hyp-goal-run, and the thing under test is hyp-goal-run's review/budget text; check lines 1-5 against that (e.g. can a replayed runner's own stop clause differ per rival, so line 2 compares unlike things? is line 3 decidable when a review has no probes? does line 5's mean with a max-cost hang substitution behave for a cell where status-quo trials hang?). (e) preflight: scan the stores and docs this change touches for any claim the run would contradict (e.g. a doc saying hyp states no run cap, a prompt text hard-coded in prompt_test.go).\nCheck every fact against the source before reporting it; say which file and line. Report under: BREAKS (with the scenario), UNDECIDABLE, CONTRADICTIONS, OWNER DECISIONS the grill must ask now, and CONFIRMED-OK. Be concise (under 700 words). Do not propose new features beyond fixing a broken rule."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3532,"cache_read_input_tokens":84764,"output_tokens":3685,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1653},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3532,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3685,"cache_read_input_tokens":84764,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3532,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3532},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fall