+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XMQ8Q632FWZ3Q1F17VMA","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:23.432593Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XMQ8Q632FWZ3Q1F17VMA","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781XDT3C72ZAXYM24QJXJT3","title":"H-name-at-stop: the stop checkpoint names each candidate without a review","body":"Keep a review as its own Experiment; the stop checkpoint names every candidate with no review, so the gap is visible. Also tested combined with each single that fails line 1 alone.","alias":"h-name-at-stop"},"why":"A rival of issue #141 named by the owner, to be tested from the cuts."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XMQYDCZ2XEYFRRB8H98M","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:23.454015Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XMQYDCZ2XEYFRRB8H98M","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781XDT3C72ZAXYM24QJXJT3","title":"H-reserve-last: with one Result left the run reviews the current candidate, not another fix","body":"The run stops with the review's findings recorded as limits, not with a new commit.","alias":"h-reserve-last"},"why":"A rival of issue #141 named by the owner, to be tested from the cuts."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XMRKM32ZWP6T7PQB7E71","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:23.475606Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XMRKM32ZWP6T7PQB7E71","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781XDT3C72ZAXYM24QJXJT3","title":"H-raise-budget: the default of --experiments rises to fit a gate and a review per candidate","body":"A scratch change to prompt.go's default (for example 7). Run 2 argues against it: each review so far led to a new commit.","alias":"h-raise-budget"},"why":"A rival of issue #141 named by the owner, to be tested from the cuts."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XMS8D3KRKJY2W0MSQPSP","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:23.496225Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XMS8D3KRKJY2W0MSQPSP","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781XDT3C72ZAXYM24QJXJT3","title":"H-probe-closes: a case the run's own probe passed on the candidate is closed in the review's Result, not a limit","body":"A limit stays for a case no check ran or one the candidate fails. Run 3's N1 and P1 would close on 3cfd08d with no further commit.","alias":"h-probe-closes"},"why":"A rival of issue #141 named by the owner, to be tested from the cuts."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XMSWGX00DMBTGATT3AAP","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:23.516269Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XMSWGX00DMBTGATT3AAP","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781XDT3C72ZAXYM24QJXJT3","title":"H-whole-candidate: the review before the select reads the cumulative diff from the Goal's base","body":"The owner expects it to lose on cost, since one cumulative review is large; it is tested anyway.","alias":"h-whole-candidate"},"why":"A rival of issue #141 named by the owner, to be tested from the cuts."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XMTHF1838ADNWWY7QCEM","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:23.537386Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XMTHF1838ADNWWY7QCEM","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781XDT3C72ZAXYM24QJXJT3","title":"H-review-owed: hyp status OWED lists a review for a candidate that has none","body":"A scratch hyp binary derives the owed review from the log. A gate and a review look alike (--recipe none --rubric reading); if the log cannot tell them apart without a new stored field, the run states the field and refers it, and adds none.","alias":"h-review-owed"},"why":"A rival of issue #141 named by the owner, to be tested from the cuts."}
