asks you nothing that you must answer, reply with exactly <<END>> and nothing else.\n\nYour positions for this issue follow.\nIssue #141: the last candidate of a budget-bound build run goes unreviewed.\n\n- Where the Goal goes: a new Goal in the existing store that already holds the history it is about, because this issue is part of #113.\n- The rivals: put every candidate fix under one question and test them all. If the grill proposes an extra rival in which hyp itself works out from the log that a review is still owed, you agree to test it. You expect the rival that reviews the whole candidate at once to lose, because one cumulative review costs a lot; you would like it treated as the expected loser.\n- The test method: replayed runs on Sonnet, 3 trials for each candidate and each starting point. You wonder whether the ak-context-engineering skill could help with how to evaluate; ask about it once.\n- Your two aims: a review must not easily run out of the run's budget, and a review must not go on and on because of small changes. Ask how each proposed line serves these two aims if the grill does not say.\n- Cost: a candidate may cost at most 1.5 times what the base costs at the same starting point. Ask how cost is computed. If the grill speaks of a median, ask how it is computed. Accept that a trial that hangs counts as the most expensive.\n- You do not want a full replay of a whole build from its start for every trial; it costs too much.\n- If the grill finds that one of its own earlier proposals was wrong and shows why, agree to drop it.\n"],"tools":[],"cliPrefix":"You are a Claude agent, built on Anthropic's Claude Agent SDK.","reminderFold":false,"systemTurns":true,"toolChangeHeader":true,"inlineTools":true,"keptReminders":true,"echoWireToolInputs":true,"contextRendering":"announced"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"734f96a5-0129-40ac-bb62-317dab6b7eaa","timestamp":"2026-11-12T14:09:15.250Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/Users/datguy/.hyp-san