@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781X3FYZF0PR6S3G0TMT5CK","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:05.790275Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781X3FYZF0PR6S3G0TMT5CK","payload":{"kind":"DesignQuestion","parent":"01M781WGMSN4QZKK8M2ERHHBWJ","title":"Which change makes a budget-bound run end with its last candidate reviewed or named, with no review loop?","body":"Scenario: replay from store cut R-8JQPWG (repository b4f23b2, actor claude-g113-1; one Result left under the base, a fix pending) and from cut R-JHBCWS (repository 3cfd08d, actor claude-g113-3; case N1 passes its probe), 3 Sonnet trials for each rival and the base. A rival is a commit that changes hyp-goal-run and, where needed, the stop clause. The base is the baseline of lines 1, 2 and 4, not a rival. Rivals can combine, only if no single rival holds the lines; the tree says which hold alone. The stop clause counts Results, not Experiments.","alias":"q-review-budget"},"why":"The issue #141 question: one DesignQuestion for every candidate fix, as the owner decided in the grill."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XA1KNPBHT0KY9R7K4J8S","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:12.499862Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XA1KNPBHT0KY9R7K4J8S","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781X3FYZF0PR6S3G0TMT5CK","title":"A candidate's review is part of its gate Result","body":"One Result carries the gate's test verdicts and the review's limits, so a candidate costs one Result again. The stop clause counts Results, so a second Result under the same Experiment would not save budget.","alias":"h-one-experiment"},"why":"Rival under the one DesignQuestion for issue #141."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XA2CF1PTKY38AXHPBZ62","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:12.524893Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XA2CF1PTKY38AXHPBZ62","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781X3FYZF0PR6S3G0TMT5CK","title":"The stop checkpoint names each candidate without a review","body":"Keep the practice of a gate and a review per candidate. The stop checkpoint names every candidate that has no review Result, so the owner sees the gap. This rival gives line 1 its floor, and it does not make a review reachable.","alias":"h-name-at-stop"},"why":"Rival under the one DesignQuestion for issue #141."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XA34CQJDJNFQJ0H48P67","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:12.548694Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XA34CQJDJNFQJ0H48P67","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781X3FYZF0PR6S3G0TMT5CK","title":"With one Result left, review the current candidate instead of committing another fix","body":"When one Result remains, the run reviews the current candidate instead of committing a fix, records the findings as limits, and stops. The run does not end on an unreviewed commit.","alias":"h-reserve-last"},"why":"Rival under the one DesignQuestion for issue #141."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XA3XYQJVRZV8HCSNDC51","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:12.573184Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XA3XYQJVRZV8HCSNDC51","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781X3FYZF0PR6S3G0TMT5CK","title":"Raise the default of --experiments to fit a gate and a review per candidate","body":"hyp prompt prints a higher default, for example 7. The owner argued from run 2 that a fixed budget still ends unreviewed while each review leads to a commit; this rival tests that argument.","alias":"h-raise-budget"},"why":"Rival under the one DesignQuestion for issue #141."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XA4K4PCBZADSH9PKQWDS","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:12.59552Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XA4K4PCBZADSH9PKQWDS","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781X3FYZF0PR6S3G0TMT5CK","title":"A case the run's own probe ran and passed closes in the review's Result, not as a limit","body":"A case that the run's own probe runs and passes on the candidate is closed in the review's Result, because a check ran it. A limit stays for a case no check ran or one the candidate fails. No commit follows a passing case.","alias":"h-probe-closes"},"why":"Rival under the one DesignQuestion for issue #141."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XA5C8NVVFN3ETV1YNXMR","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:12.620551Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"node.add","node":"01M781XA5C8NVVFN3ETV1YNXMR","payload":{"kind":"Hypothesis","parent":"01M781X3FYZF0PR6S3G0TMT5CK","title":"The review before the select reads the cumulative diff from the Goal's base","body":"The review reads the whole candidate against the lines, not the latest increment. The owner expects it to lose on cost; the run tests that and does not assume it.","alias":"h-whole-candidate"},"why":"Rival under the one DesignQuestion for issue #141."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XA65P8R7SCWAJCYSH0R0","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:12.645733Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"edge.add","node":"01M781WGMSN4QZKK8M2ERHHBWJ","payload":{"type":"external_ref","to":"https://github.com/dat9uy/hyp/issues/141"},"why":"The issue this Goal serves."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XA6YV4NFQFDGQQ0DFY9R","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:12.670802Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"edge.add","node":"01M781WGMSN4QZKK8M2ERHHBWJ","payload":{"type":"external_ref","to":"https://github.com/dat9uy/hyp/issues/113"},"why":"The issue this Goal is part of."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M781XG15C3P5QXSGN516RY01","ts":"2026-11-12T14:17:18.629441Z","actor":"claude-grill-141","type":"checkpoint","node":"01M781WGMSN4QZKK8M2ERHHBWJ","payload":{"summary":"Grill done: 6 lines written by owner-standin, line 6 citing G-ZBM2RE#1-#5 and #7. Q-TMT5CK holds six rivals (H-one-experiment, H-name-at-stop, H-reserve-last, H-raise-budget, H-probe-closes, H-whole-candidate), tested against each other and the base from the cuts R-8JQPWG and R-JHBCWS. Out-of-Goal: a typed review marker so hyp can warn on an unreviewed candidate (not derivable from the log today)."},"why":"end of grill"}
