tle \"A budget-bound run ends with its last candidate reviewed or named, and a review does not loop\" \\\n  --body $'Builds a change to the run practice of a Goal whose candidate is a commit, for issue #141 (part of #113): a run that reaches its budget has a review Result for its final candidate or names it unreviewed, and a review does not go on over small changes. The candidate is a hyp commit: skills/hyp-goal-run/SKILL.md and, where a rival needs it, the stop clause in internal/cli/prompt.go with its test and golden. One DesignQuestion holds six rivals (H-one-experiment, H-name-at-stop, H-reserve-last, H-raise-budget, H-probe-closes, H-whole-candidate), tested against each other and the base; H-whole-candidate is the expected loser. A combination is added only if no single rival holds the lines. Method: replayed runs on Sonnet (claude-sonnet-5-5), 3 trials for each candidate and each start, from two starts: store cut R-8JQPWG with repository commit b4f23b2, and store cut R-JHBCWS with repository commit 3cfd08d, each under the original actor and with the candidate\\'s own hyp prompt default. No replay of a whole build. Cost: input-equivalent tokens from the start to the stop, subagent turns included, weights input 1, cache-write 1.25, cache-read 0.1, output 5; the median of 3 trials; a hang costs infinity, and the hang cap is fixed in the Experiment\\'s verdict rule before the run. Matched base and candidate runs follow ak-context-engineering; missing telemetry is unknown.\\nMay change: this repository, in commits on the branch feat/review-budget from main; the run may push that branch and open or update one PR, and never merges it. It changes skills/hyp-goal-run/SKILL.md, internal/cli/prompt.go with its tests and golden, and the texts the change makes wrong: skills/hyp-owner-grill/SKILL.md (the hand-off\\'s default budget), docs/how-hyp-improves-itself.md (the run cap), and docs/replay-spec.md, docs/glossary.md and README.md where they state the stop clause.\\nRead only: plans/, every investigations/ tree except goal-prompt, ak-skill-creator under .claude/skills, and ak-context-engineering under /Users/datguy/.agentkit/cache/kits/engineer/claude-code/3.0.0/engineer/skills/ak-context-engineering (SKILL.md sha256 ad2ce02b31b8d0595a934267ce726b489044443711f75622a7199e13e88d6383, references/evaluation.md sha256 fdd4a34ff3d1b937ad482a031160b8b9da40f73a20244258d6d38e77ed8d2d0b).\\nNever: commit to main or merge a PR.\\nNever: replace ~/.local/bin/hyp or ~/.local/share/hyp/hyp-33896ec; compile the candidate to a separate path.\\nNever: edit recipes/, rubrics/, another investigations/ tree, ak-skill-creator, ak-context-engineering or another repository.\\nNever: write under an owner\\'s actor; if a step needs the owner, refer with a reason or record a reading, and stop.' \\\n  --line \"[P] At store cut R-8JQPWG with repository commit b4f23b2, under actor claude-g113-1 and the candidate's own hyp prompt default, each of 3 Sonnet trials ends with a review Result for its final candidate or a stop checkpoint that names that candidate as unreviewed. The baseline skill (sha256 a6152711c2c930b275583f19dec074205e3eb83deac8d361831fda3566b080ab) does neither in at least one of 3 trials, and the candidate differs from it.\" \\\n  --line \"[P] At store cut R-JHBCWS with repository commit 3cfd08d, under actor claude-g113-3, where the review case N1 passes its probe, each of 3 Sonnet trials ends with the select of H-FQ103R and records no later candidate commit. The baseline skill (sha256 cb15e2f2e207b5a66807c9369e4d776d5378e61c2dd99679c36dfba402fa750e) records a later commit in at least one of 3 trials, and the candidate differs from it.\" \\\n  --line \"[N] From either store cut, no trial records more than 2 fresh-reviewer runs before the select or the stop.\" \\\n  --line \"[N] At either store cut, a candidate's median trial cost exceeds 1.5 times the base's median, or it has 2 or more hangs in 3 trials. Cost is input-equivalent tokens from th