-skill-creator or another repository.\nNever: write under an owner's actor; if a step needs the owner, refer with a reason or record a reading, and stop.\nline G-ZBM2RE#1 covered on Q-Z93VJ5; ran in R-KPWZZC, R-50GBXM, R-FRF929, R-28A8NB, R-356DV0, R-27Y1EV, R-BSWFXG — [P] For a Goal whose body holds a valid constraints block, hyp prompt <G> --actor A exits 0 and prints the same bytes on every call for the same log and flags: the store's path relative to the repository root, A, G, the skill hyp-goal-run, the stop clauses (the line \"runner owes nothing\", or N Results recorded under A, N from --experiments, default 5), and each block line byte for byte in body order. --branch and --pr only add clauses after the block.\nline G-ZBM2RE#2 covered on Q-Z93VJ5; ran in R-KPWZZC, R-50GBXM, R-FRF929, R-28A8NB, R-356DV0, R-27Y1EV, R-BSWFXG — [N] hyp prompt prints no text of an owner answer: its output for a Goal is byte-identical before and after an answer event is added to the log.\nline G-ZBM2RE#3 covered on Q-Z93VJ5; ran in R-KPWZZC, R-50GBXM, R-FRF929, R-28A8NB, R-356DV0, R-27Y1EV, R-BSWFXG — [N] The constraints block runs from the first line that starts with \"May change:\", \"Read only:\" or \"Never:\" to the end of the body. hyp prompt exits 1 and prints nothing to stdout when the block is missing, lacks one of the three headings, or holds a non-empty line that starts with none of them, naming each missing heading or the bad line. hyp add goal still accepts such a body with exit 0, and warns when the body has a heading but no valid block.\nline G-ZBM2RE#4 covered on Q-Z93VJ5; ran in R-KPWZZC, R-50GBXM, R-FRF929, R-28A8NB, R-356DV0, R-27Y1EV, R-BSWFXG — [N] In a store with two Goals, where one answer event settles a key of each, hyp prompt G prints the same bytes as for G's events in a store of their own.\nline G-ZBM2RE#5 covered on Q-Z93VJ5; ran in R-KPWZZC, R-50GBXM, R-FRF929, R-28A8NB, R-356DV0, R-27Y1EV, R-BSWFXG — [N] hyp prompt with no --actor exits 2 and never fa