t be replayed from this cut. The limit already exists there, and only a later Result can close it.\n   - SKILL.md:69 defines a limit as \"a case the Goal covers that no check ran\". It closes only through a test within the Goal's lines. An uncontained probe script is not that.\n   - \"A check ran it\" is not decidable from the log. The probe sits in `evidence/`, outside any recipe.\n\n3. **The cut after R-8JQPWG does not reproduce \"one Result left\" unless the actor and `--experiments` are fixed.**\n   - claude-g113-1 recorded 4 Results by that cut (R-KPWZZC, R-9V3ER0, R-50GBXM, R-8JQPWG), checked from `.tree/events`.\n   - The cut itself holds no count. A replayed run under a fresh actor has 5 left. Under claude-g113-1 with the default of 5, it has 1 left.\n   - L1 names neither the actor nor the flag. The clause counts only \"Results recorded under A\" (`internal/cli/prompt.go`, near line 150), and I found nothing in the code that enforces it.\n\n4. **The unit is Results, but the issue and the lines speak of Experiments.** Run 1 recorded 6 Results against its 5. R-FRF929 and R-9EGPYD both have parent NZR3GV, so one Experiment produced two Results. \"One Result carries gate and review\" (H-one-experiment) does not guarantee one unit of budget. L1 and L4 never say which unit counts.\n\n5. **L6 and H-raise-budget collide with the closed Goal's line 1.**\n   - G-ZBM2RE#1 pins \"N Results recorded under A, N from --experiments, default 5\".\n   - `prompt_test.go:55` and `internal/cli/testdata/prompt-fixture/prompt.golden:2` pin the exact clause bytes. Any change to the default or the wording means editing the golden file and the test.\n   - So \"lines 1-5 still hold\" is false by construction for H-raise-budget, and for H-name-at-stop if it adds a clause to the printed stop.\n   - Line 6 is dropped from L6, but its fixture is the same golden prompt.\n   - Replay-spec rule 32 (line 134) refuses a close or aim whose key leads to another Goal. The new Goal cannot record G-ZBM2RE#n as closed.\n   - L6 can only be a line of the new Goal that cites those lines (rule 31). Writing that line is the owner's job, per SKILL.md:75.\n   - Because G-ZBM2RE is complete, nothing re-runs its lines. L6 is a cite plus `go test`.\n\n6. **The base moves (scenario c), and \"the base skill\" is ambiguous.**\n   - Main is now 9c8e498, and the pending fix 5c5902d and its successors are already in it (git log).\n   - A replay based on main finds the limits G1, G2 and G8 already fixed, so nothing is left to separate the base from the candidate.\n   - A replay based on b4f23b2 installs that commit's SKILL.md, not main's. AGENTS.md also says skill text and the host's agent files reach replayed runs.\n   - So L1's \"base skill (sha256)\" must name which file, and the candidate must be overlaid on b4f23b2 or the cut moved. The Goal does not say.\n\n7. **L4 cannot be decided from the store.**\n   - Token counts, hangs and \"fresh-reviewer runs\" (L3) live in transcripts. The log holds only the Results.\n   - A candidate that adds a review will cost more than a base that stops after a fix. The base stops early because it skips the review, which is the defect. 1.5x on a short remaining tail is likely to fail on a legitimate fix.\n   - Whether subagent tokens count is not stated.\n   - For H-raise-budget at the one-left cut, forcing `--experiments 1` hides the changed default. Leaving the default in place gives the candidate more room than the base, so the costs are not comparable.\n\n8. **Two Goals in one store.**\n   - The skill already says to run `hyp status <goal-id>` (SKILL.md:12).\n   - A cut taken after R-8JQPWG predates the new Goal's own events. The replayed run sees only G-ZBM2RE, never the new Goal's lines or the Q-A/Q-B/Q-C rivals.\n   - The cut run therefore tests the skill against the old Goal's lines, not the new ones, so L5 (the text states how reviews are recorded) is unobservable there.\n\n9. **The Goal's own run (d) uses the unchanged skill and the default of 5.** It will probably hit the same stop. It needs a candidate commit, a gate, a review and fixes. Each review so far has led to a new commit (issue comment 1: findings 10, 8, 1, 2). L3 limits fresh-reviewer runs inside trials only, not the Goal's own run. The Goal should say how the run itself is budgeted, for example `--experiments`.\n\n10. **Merged log from two actors (b).** Nothing in the clause or the planned lines covers a reviewer subagent that writes under its own actor. SKILL.md:34 does not say which actor records the review Result, so \"counts against the budget\" (L5) is ambiguous. The ledger counts by actor, so a review recorded under another actor would not count.\n\nI found no contradiction in L3's wording on \"more than 2\" runs. I did not check the sha256 values themselves, or whether `hyp record` accepts a `--closes` without a new aim."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","totalDurationMs":126127,"totalTokens":71090,"totalToolUseCount":14,"usage":{"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1798},"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3928,"cache_read_input_tokens":63098,"output_tokens":4062,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3928},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4062,"cache_read_input_tokens":63098,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3928,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"toolStats":{"readCount":1,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":13,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0},"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ef3af7b7-8df3-41e3-8e8b-1a050ead8727","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"rule","ruleSource":"cliArg"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/Users/datguy