+{"v":1,"id":"01M782F0SMXXWW50293VN77C5E","ts":"2026-11-12T14:26:52.85216Z","actor":"owner-standin","type":"node.add","node":"01M782F0SMXXWW50293VN77C5E","payload":{"kind":"Goal","parent":"","title":"hyp prints a run's /goal prompt from the log, and a Goal body records the run's constraints","body":"Builds #113: `hyp prompt` prints a run's /goal prompt from the log; the constraints block below is its read side. Owner decision 2026-11-11: constraints live in the body under May change:, Read only: and Never:, and a typed field waits until a real run misreads or loses one. Every block line needs text after its colon. One checker serves `hyp add goal` (warns, still appends) and `hyp prompt` (refuses, exit 1). hyp prints the run cap and never enforces it; ADR 0022 supersedes ADR 0017's cap line in part. Lines 8 and 9 are an ak-skill-creator eval of the hyp-owner-grill Hand off: 2 cases, 3 Sonnet trials each, candidate and base skill, graded by eval_skill.py. The description edits have no line and no routing traces run: a known gap. A commit Goal's other needs from hyp are #114.\nMay change: this repository (hyp): commits on one local branch\nMay change: one pull request, opened and never merged\nMay change: internal/cli and internal/replay for the command and the shared block checker\nMay change: the descriptions of hyp-goal-run and hyp-prototype, which name one Goal kind\nMay change: skills/hyp-owner-grill Hand off, and the block definition in each skill that states it\nMay change: README.md, docs/glossary.md, docs/replay-spec.md, docs/core-and-self-review.md, docs/how-hyp-improves-itself.md\nMay change: a new docs/adr/0022, and a new recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval@1\nRead only: investigations/checkpoint-store and the other published trees\nRead only: the ak-skill-creator skill, named on the eval command's External: line and never copied\nNever: replace the installed ~/.local/bin/hyp\nNever: edit a stored Goal or event\nNever: add a typed constraints field to `hyp add goal`\nNever: store a Result count, an actor baseline or a parsed constraint field","lines":[{"text":"[P] For a valid block, `hyp prompt G --actor A` exits 0 and prints: `/goal Run the hyp tree in \"\u003cstore path\u003e\" with the hyp-goal-run skill, as HYP_ACTOR=A. Its Goal is G.` / `First run `hyp status G` there; if no such Goal shows, stop.` / `Done when the latest `hyp status G` shows `runner owes nothing: stop and report to the owner` under OWED, or 5 Results have been recorded under A, or you cannot take the next step honestly and say why.` / `At each stop, record the stop checkpoint the skill names, and list the lines under LINES with the Results that ran them.` / the block, line for line."},{"text":"[P] `--results N` changes only the 5. `--branch B` adds exactly `Commit only to branch B.` and `--pr P` adds exactly `Do not merge PR #P.`, each as one line after the block, and nothing else changes."},{"text":"[P] The output depends only on the merged log and the flags: the same bytes for any order of the actors' events files. `hyp prompt` appends no event and changes no file. The Results counted are the actor's recorded Results under this Goal; a retracted one does not count."},{"text":"[N] A Goal with no valid block (no heading, a missing heading, a bare heading with no text after its colon, or a non-empty line in the block that starts with no heading) makes `hyp prompt` exit 1, name the missing heading or the first bad line, and print nothing on stdout. CRLF line ends read as LF."},{"text":"[P] `hyp add goal` with a body that has no heading, or a heading but no valid block, appends the Goal, exits 0 and prints a `warn:` line that names the rule and the first bad line. A body with a valid block prints no warning. One checker serves both commands."},{"text":"[N] Bad arguments exit 2: an invalid actor, a `--pr` that is not digits, a `--branch` with whitespace, a control character or a leading `-`, a `--results` below 1, and an id that is not a Goal. No repository holding the store exits 3. `hyp prompt -h` exits 0 with no store."},{"text":"[N] `hyp prompt` for an actor that already wrote any event in the store exits 1, names the rule and tells the owner to choose a new actor."},{"text":"[P] At the candidate, each of 3 fresh Sonnet trials of the hyp-owner-grill Hand off, given a finished grill whose Goal has a valid block, ends with the output of `hyp prompt` for that Goal byte for byte and adds no sentence."},{"text":"[N] At the candidate, no one of 3 fresh Sonnet trials of the Hand off, given a Goal that `hyp prompt` refuses, writes a prompt by hand. Each tells the owner of the refusal."}]},"why":"Owner flow, #113: grilled 2026-11-12; constraints live in the body, a typed field waits."}
+{"v":1,"id":"01M782GZFY74CNTAQQ99HEDGTC","ts":"2026-11-12T14:27:57.05427Z","actor":"owner-standin","type":"node.add","node":"01M782GZFY74CNTAQQ99HEDGTC","payload":{"kind":"Goal","parent":"","title":"Design record for #113: who prints a run's /goal prompt, and what hyp does on a Goal with no valid constraints block","body":"Records three questions the owner settled by argument in the grill session of 2026-11-12, with the session as evidence. G-N77C5E builds the design and carries its cases as lines. No run checks these candidates, so this Goal has no lines.\nMay change: this Goal's tree events and evidence, to record the session's decisions\nRead only: the repository\nNever: run this Goal as an unattended /goal"},"why":"Owner flow, #113: design record split from its build, per the grill skill."}
