or closed: whether its case ran is per candidate, its coverage. `Open()` of a line means only that its hand is not an accept. **Coverage**: a Result covers a Hypothesis when it has a verdict on it, or when one of the Result's run subjects holds the Hypothesis's whole subject (§4 subject; `Projection.Covers`). Coverage says the bytes ran, not that the claim held. A line is **covered** on a question when a closer of the line covers each of its candidates, and **uncovered** there otherwise. An unaccepted, unreferred line is owed on each live top-level question where it is uncovered (`Projection.Uncovered`), so a new candidate is owed the line again. Coverage is not a state of the move table: it changes when a candidate is added or falls, with no move on the key, and no move reads it. `hyp show G-…#n` prints the line's text, its hand when it has one (`hand: accepted by o`), each cite with what it meant and, when that differs, what it would mean now (`cites H-…: realised, now unsettled`), each top-level question's candidates with `covered` or `uncovered: H-…`, each closer with what it ran on (`ran in R-…: ran on H-… (alias): supports; ran on H-…`), the aiming Experiments and the history. A verdict is per Hypothesis, never per line: a Result that closes several lines and contradicts H says the cases ran and H failed, not which line, so nothing prints `fails <line>`. `hyp status` prints a LINES section under the GOAL line, one line each with its facts joined by `; `, each only when it has one: its hand, `covered on Q-…, Q-…` and `uncovered on Q-…: H-…` for each live top-level question with a candidate, and `ran in R-…`; a line with none prints `no candidate`. Neither `open` nor `closed` prints for a line. The section also prints and the mark `(no one closer covers H-… and H-… together)` when the Hypotheses selected on two or more top-level questions were never covered by one closer (`Projection.NotTogether`); a claim that depends on its host is covered only together with i