+{"v":1,"id":"01M782A00343Y3KNWK017RHQKG","ts":"2026-11-12T14:24:08.195747Z","actor":"owner-standin","type":"node.add","node":"01M782A00343Y3KNWK017RHQKG","payload":{"kind":"Goal","parent":"","title":"Decide how a run reviews each candidate commit of a build Goal within its budget","body":"Decide, by replaying two cuts of this store, which rule text lets the run of a build Goal keep every candidate commit reviewed within its Result budget, without reviews that continue because of small changes. Part of #113; the event and the rivals are in issue #141. The candidates are rule texts for skills/hyp-goal-run, given as throwaway patches over its text at sha256 cb15e2f2e207b5a66807c9369e4d776d5378e61c2dd99679c36dfba402fa750e, and the --experiments default. The status quo is the baseline. The run ends at the select; the build of the chosen rule is another Goal.\n\nTrials: the cut after R-8JQPWG (candidate 5c5902d, fix 2284172 pending) and the cut after R-JHBCWS (candidate 3cfd08d, fix d2d5d14 pending). Each rival gets 3 trials on each cut, and the status quo gets 3 on each cut. Each trial uses a fresh actor, runs on Sonnet from the cut and its candidate commit, and stops on the prompt clause or after 60 minutes. No trial replays a build from its start. The cost of a trial is the Results recorded under its actor from the cut to its stop; a hung trial counts the highest cost of any trial on that cut that did not hang. The cost of a rule on a cut is the median of its 3 trial costs, taken for each cut alone. The drive.json token and dollar cost is reported and decides nothing.\n\nMay change: this tree's events and evidence in investigations/goal-prompt/.tree, and scratch sandboxes and trial actors\nRead only: skills/, internal/, docs/ and the other trees of this repository\nNever: edit skills/ or docs/, replace an installed binary, push a branch, open or merge a PR","lines":[{"text":"[N] On the cut after R-8JQPWG or the cut after R-JHBCWS, a run under the rule stops with a candidate commit that has no review Result, and its stop checkpoint does not name that candidate as unreviewed."},{"text":"[P] The rule text states how a review of a candidate commit is recorded (which Experiment, which Result, which verdict) and whether that review counts against the stop clause."},{"text":"[N] A review Result closes as passing a case that no check ran, or a case that the candidate fails."},{"text":"[N] A run stops with a finding of a review that is not sorted: not a limit, not a close by a check that ran its case, not a fix commit, not a reading, and not an out-of-Goal finding named in the stop checkpoint."},{"text":"[P] On the cut after R-JHBCWS, when every finding of a review of 3cfd08d is a case that a probe the run itself ran already passes on 3cfd08d, the run closes those cases by that probe and writes no further candidate commit."},{"text":"[P] On the cut after R-8JQPWG, the run stops with its final candidate commit having a review Result."},{"text":"[N] A candidate rule that differs from the status-quo rule (skills/hyp-goal-run/SKILL.md, sha256 cb15e2f2e207b5a66807c9369e4d776d5378e61c2dd99679c36dfba402fa750e) and costs more than 1.5 times its cost on the same cut is admitted. Cost is the median of 3 trials, each the Results recorded under its actor from the cut to its stop; a hung trial counts the highest cost of any non-hung trial on that cut."}]},"why":"issue 141: runs 1 to 3 of the goal-prompt tree ended with a candidate unreviewed or with reviews that each led to another commit"}
